title: Declarative decorator table shared by parser/typer/docs
status: complete
atomic: true
priority: low
blocked_by: []
created_at: '2026-06-10T05:18:42'
updated_at: '2026-06-13T14:03:17'
result: 'Created src/store_decorators.rs as the single declarative source of truth:
  const STORE_DECORATORS/FIELD_DECORATORS tables encoding each decorator''s name,
  argument arity/type (None/Int/Ident), mutual exclusions, numeric-only field constraints,
  and doc summary. Parser (actor_store.rs) now validates names + argument shapes +
  store-level exclusions from the table; typer (lower/decl.rs) validates field type
  constraints (@unique on f64 rejected, @increment requires numeric) and field exclusions.
  render_docs() generates the decorator reference from the same table. Nonsensical
  combos (@kv+@vector, @mem+@versioned, @unique on f64, unknown decorators) produce
  precise diagnostics. Pinned by tests/store_decorator_table.rs (7 conformance tests)
  + 9 module unit tests including a sync invariant (every AST variant in table) and
  exclusion symmetry. Full lib suite (249), all store suites, std_stable_subset, access_semantics
  green; zero new warnings.'
description: Item 12. One table (name, arg arity/type, applicability store-vs-field,
  mutual exclusions) consumed by parser, typer validation, and docs gen. Reject nonsensical
  combos (@kv+@vector, @mem+@versioned, @unique on f64) with precise diagnostics.
